    "result_text": "All 284 tests pass with a green build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit in the `addOwner` method of `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`.\n\n**Change** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\nAfter the new owner's registration date is resolved (defaulting to today when not supplied), the controller counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today. If 20 or more owners have already been registered today, it returns `400 Bad Request` before persisting:\n\n```java\nlong ownersRegisteredToday = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()\n    .filter(existing -> LocalDate.now().equals(existing.getRegistrationDate()))\n    .count();\nif (ownersRegisteredToday >= 20) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);\n}\n```\n\n**Tests** (`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`): added two cases \u2014\n- `createOwnerRejectedWhenDailyLimitReached`: 20 owners registered today \u2192 21st POST returns 400.\n- `createOwnerAllowedWhenBelowDailyLimit`: 19 owners registered today \u2192 next POST still returns 201.\n\nSeed owners have a null registration date so they don't count toward the limit, and the class is `@Transactional` so each test rolls back cleanly.",
